            <div xml:id="d1071">

                <pb facs="0983" n="669" xml:id="pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.741/58</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-07">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your 265. The President issued an Executive order on August 5 prohibiting all
                    radio stations within the jurisdiction of the United States from transmitting or
                    receiving for delivery messages in cipher or of an unneutral nature, and from in
                    any way rendering to any one of the belligerents any unneutral service, during
                    the continuance of hostilities. The Secretary of the Navy is strictly enforcing
                    this order.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
